    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0075" n="65" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg65"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/543: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Castleman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-06T14:00:00-06:00">September 6, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>96. For Duggan.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d56-f1"/> Cramp and I have arranged by
                    telephone that the Foreign Offices of Nicaragua and Honduras are to talk by
                    telephone <pb facs="0076" n="66" xml:id="pg66"/> at 4 this afternoon to arrange
                    simultaneous presentation of assurances that troops will not be moved, covering
                    the following points: hour of presentations, form and extent of assurances,
                    appropriate publicity.</p>
                <p>We will telegraph after the interview.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castleman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d56-f1" n="24" xml:id="d56-f1-content">
                <p>Laurence Duggan, Chief of the Division of the American Republics.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
